      "id": 1,
      "text": "Homeland Park was established in the early twentieth century as a mill village for the Anderson Cotton Mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/south-carolina_homeland-park"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community is named Homeland Park to reflect its origins as a planned residential area for mill workers and their families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/south-carolina_homeland-park"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Homeland Park is a suburban area in central Anderson County located south of the city of Anderson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeland_Park%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Murray Avenue serves as the main north-south road running through the Homeland Park community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeland_Park%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route twenty-nine leads southwest out of Homeland Park and reaches the Georgia border in fourteen miles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeland_Park%2C_South_Carolina"
    },
    {
